      "statement": "Assistant-executed local verification at exact subject b04a2e1b724faed558b1cbdd68188ec6c7fee2f7, tree fb645fc0a63c5029a2bcf1dc12b5dc5f8d3e6652, in a clean standalone clone with Python 3.12 and pinned requirements-evals.txt dependencies. Source integrates main 80f53905f793751aa47ed4093d5dd035cab608ff. Full repository discovery ran 460 tests, 459 passed and one skipped; all 9 receipt guard tests passed; 4/4 positive fixtures accepted and 11/11 adversarial fixtures rejected for intended rules. Generated validation report SHA-256 7e9f889ab6f502c0b7f9f99c658ce550734ab06c40bcddba58691e5ea2031962 and generated CI-style binding both name this exact execution head. Candidate agent conformance and Golden candidate merge checks passed; the 16 existing admission holds remain unresolved. Four regression tests demonstrated prior-head report relabelling, leftover success after a blocked invocation, acceptance of a non-candidate report and untracked candidate source on original code, then passed with the fix. Generated outputs were untracked execution artifacts; tracked source remained clean. Initial environment lacked jsonschema; dependencies were installed before successful fixture runs. Report/receipt digests are provenance bindings, not authenticated independent review. No hosted CI pass: retry of old-head workflow 41298767527 attempt 2 job 124871775406 failed with runner_id=0, no steps and account-billing-lock annotation. Hosted infrastructure gate and required-check/protection confirmation remain unmet. Human approval, beneficiary value, retention, closure, scalability, compounding, runtime and Canon admission are not established.",
